## 🎯 Project Objectives

The main objectives of this project are to:

- Understand the structure of a real-world dataset
- Perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
- Identify missing values
- Handle missing data appropriately
- Identify numerical and categorical features
- Detect potential outliers
- Create meaningful data visualizations
- Analyze relationships between features and passenger survival
- Develop the habit of interpreting data before applying machine learning models

---

## 📂 Dataset

The project uses the **Titanic: Machine Learning from Disaster** dataset.

The dataset contains information about Titanic passengers, including:

- Passenger ID
- Survival status
- Passenger class
- Name
- Gender
- Age
- Number of siblings/spouses
- Number of parents/children
- Ticket
- Fare
- Cabin
- Embarked port

The training dataset contains **891 rows and 12 columns**.

