---

## 🔍 Key Findings

Some important observations from the analysis include:

- The dataset contains both numerical and categorical features.
- `Age`, `Cabin`, and `Embarked` originally contained missing values.
- `Cabin` had a particularly large amount of missing data.
- The `Fare` variable contains several potential high-value outliers.
- Survival rates differ substantially between male and female passengers.
- Passenger class also shows an important relationship with survival.
- `Sex` appears to be one of the strongest features associated with survival in this dataset.

> These findings represent associations observed in the dataset and do not necessarily imply causation.

